{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/944893-anyone-here-a-fan-of-the-2011-teen-wolf","id":944893,"title":"Anyone here a fan of the 2011 Teen Wolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-06T09:25:26-07:00","id":944893,"title":"Anyone here a fan of the 2011 Teen Wolf?","content":"i wish the main character Scott McCall would spend more of his transformed states in Gauru form like Peter Hale did in most of Season 1. We are about to start the 6th and final season and Scott is usually either in Dalu or Hishu which makes me a little sad but i still love the show.<br /> <br /> Are there any Gifts that reflect Scotts powers at all like taking away pain from another living being or invading someones memories that even they don't understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T10:09:05-07:00","id":944922,"title":"","content":"There are Gifts in both editions that allow you to an ability to take the wounds of another onto yourself, and others to harass people's dreams. Straight up telepathy is more of a vampire thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:00:29-07:00","id":944983,"title":"","content":"Each Alpha appears to develop abilities and powers unique to themselves as they go. Peter Hale was and is a monstrous person so him turning into a Gauru form fits, and once he got back to fighting form at the end of season 4 he was still clearly unhinged and his form reflected that. The Hale family seems to have a unique ability to straight up turn into wolves so it could play into that.<br /> <br /> Duecalion was the Demon Wolf and his transformed self didn't look right in any sense of the word. Although getting his sight back might have fixed his mental instabilities and he may look somewhat normal.<br /> <br /> The Beast wasn't even an Alpha but was basically a Slasher as a Werewolf. No idea if this was a reflection of someone getting their Wolfness via rainwater in the paw print or just how monstrous he was as an individual. Even at their worst Peter and Duecalion weren't mass murdering people. While The Beast had entire stockpiles of corpses sitting around.<br /> <br /> Scott's unique ability appears to be something close to a Cahalith's purpose. He boosts the power of people around him and rises to the occasion by gaining strength to defend them. Although in the episode from season 4 when he was defending Mai's pack from the Hunters fulfilling the contract his face was definitely becoming more wolf-like as he fought. So I'm not sure if he's deliberately holding himself back or what.<br /> <br /> But yes, I fucking love Teen Wolf and its heavily influenced my views of Werewolf. The way the pack system works Second Edition plays even more like the show and I'm pretty sure you can get what you want from it. It probably wouldn't break anything to make a weird merit where a werewolf can focus and go into a person's mind like in the show. And if we get Second Edition version of Dreamer's Moon Gift I'd bank on that. Although the core Moon Gift appears to have swallowed most of ts thematic space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:04:47-07:00","id":945242,"title":"","content":"I feel like the show went to shit after season 3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:44:53-07:00","id":945453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/944893-anyone-here-a-fan-of-the-2011-teen-wolf?p=945242#post945242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the show went to shit after season 3</div> </div> </div> </div>i think it vastly improved, they got rid of isaac who was killing the show for me with his crybaby emo streaks and Allison who was in my opinion cool sometimes and unreasonable at others. The only character left that kind of annoys me is Malia, i liked her at first but because of her personality type her writing seems a little too predictable with the way she reacts to things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:27:13-07:00","id":945830,"title":"","content":"i liked the show far better when it was about werewolves and werewolf problems. I also liked the isaac and scott pack. I dont like that the writer for the show seems to have a hard on for mind fucks. It feels to me like he's trying too hard with the plot and that makes it nigh unwatchable. <br /> <br /> lets not forget the character progression has thus far been terrible for everyone but stiles. Scott hasn't improved at all. It feels as painful as watching gundam seed destiny, which was largely pretty damn bad. <br /> <br /> Bring me back inter pack problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:03:08-07:00","id":956662,"title":"","content":"I am literally obsessed with a Chronicles of Darkness AU that I will someday write. Its pretty embarrassing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}